{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":49.70000076293945,"text":"The Mariano Market was built in 1922, a few years after the Great Fire, on the spot where a school had burned down. It was designed by Eli Mariano, an architect from Thessaloniki's Jewish community, which had lived in the city for centuries. It is a covered market, an iron frame, a glass roof, and underneath it rows of stalls with fish, cheese, olives, spices, and small tavernas. Light comes in from above and falls down the aisles, so even in winter it needs few lamps. For a good many years, the market had almost emptied out and was close to closing for good. It was restored and opened again in 2022, with its old shell still in place. Beside it runs the Kapani, an even older market with no roof at all.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.46000000834465027},{"word":"Mariano","start":0.46000000834465027,"end":0.8999999761581421},{"word":"Market","start":0.8999999761581421,"end":1.2999999523162842},{"word":"was","start":1.2999999523162842,"end":1.6399999856948853},{"word":"built","start":1.6399999856948853,"end":1.8799999952316284},{"word":"in","start":1.8799999952316284,"end":2.200000047683716},{"word":"1922","start":2.200000047683716,"end":3.319999933242798},{"word":"a","start":3.880000114440918,"end":3.9800000190734863},{"word":"few","start":3.9800000190734863,"end":4.139999866485596},{"word":"years","start":4.139999866485596,"end":4.400000095367432},{"word":"after","start":4.400000095367432,"end":4.679999828338623},{"word":"the","start":4.679999828338623,"end":4.900000095367432},{"word":"Great","start":4.900000095367432,"end":5.159999847412109},{"word":"Fire","start":5.159999847412109,"end":5.400000095367432},{"word":"on","start":5.78000020980835,"end":5.960000038146973},{"word":"the","start":5.960000038146973,"end":6.139999866485596},{"word":"spot","start":6.139999866485596,"end":6.360000133514404},{"word":"where","start":6.360000133514404,"end":6.579999923706055},{"word":"a","sta